<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12575" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπο-ζεύγνῡμι</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>separate, part,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. συνεύνων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Man.
					3.85
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ.τὸ τείχισμα</span> Malch.<i><span class="en">
				p.412D.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> mostly in 
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ζεύγνῠμαι,</span>
			aor.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-εζύγην [ῠ</span>] (v. infr.), also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-εζεύχθην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>El.</u>
					284
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				12.226
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Strat.
			</span></i>):—<i>to be loosed from the yoke,</i> [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βοῦς] εἰς νομὰς ἀπεζεύχθη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Babr.
					37.6
				</span></i>
			; but usually metaph., <i>to be parted from,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέκνων γυναικός τ᾽</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>HF</u>
					1375
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Med.</u>
				1017
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰ γάμων ἀπεζύγην</span> if I
				<i>were free from . .,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				791
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρφανὸς ἀποζυγείς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					988
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥσπερ δεῦρ᾽ ἀπεζύγην
			πόδας</span> as I <i>unharnessed</i> my feet, i.e. took rest,
				<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				676
			</span></i>.</div>
